From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:47:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Modes round 2: permissions, splits that keep Properties,
 Architect creates, Flow only shows, Grid edits options, Intelligent validates
 and masks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One survey, five views, each with a purpose and a permission set — and
every edit through the same engine and store.

- Permission model: MODE_CAPABILITIES (build / structure / understand /
  review / assist) and propertiesWanted(mode, split). A split shows the
  Properties panel when any pane wants it: Studio + Intelligent keeps
  Display, Skip and Advanced logic (§1, §13). Clicks inside a pane, its
  head or the divider never deselect. The Questions panel scrolls to a
  selection made elsewhere (a Flow node, a Grid row, an Intelligent chip).
- Flow (§4–5): no "+ Add…", no drop-to-move; click selects, double-click
  opens Studio on the question (a no-op when Studio is already a pane);
  the inspector is read-only — summary, validation, mask, logic,
  dependencies — with Open in Studio; zoom is a typed percentage (5–300,
  Enter applies, out-of-range refused) beside −, +, Fit and 1:1.
- Architect (§2–3): + Question into the selected page or block
  (insertionPoint reads ctx.primary; a block → its last page), + Block
  after the selection, + Element (branch, randomizer, loop, quota check,
  embedded data), duplicate, ↑/↓, delete with the references dialog;
  "+ Question here" in page and container workspaces. Every one is the
  command the palette and the Questions panel run.
- Grid (§6–8): the Options cell opens a list editor (code, label, add,
  remove, reorder; Done is one undo step; existing options untouched;
  rows × columns send you to Studio); the Validation column is on by
  default. Type is never forced — the Type cell and bulk type change
  already migrate through migrateQuestionType.
- Intelligent (§9–10): validation intents (between, at least/most,
  characters, selections, email/phone/url/zip/integer, pattern, clear)
  → set_validation / clear_validation, merged by rule kind and refused
  when the kind does not fit the question or a min exceeds a max;
  masking intents ("at Q13 show only the options selected in Q11",
  "hide … from …", "carry forward …", "mask Q5 by Q3 AND Q4") → a set
  expression parsed by parseSetExpression → set_mask, the same
  OptionMask the Masking builder writes; the context lists validation
  and masks; the model contract and coercer know the new shapes.
- Engine: logicProposal gains set_validation, clear_validation,
  set_mask with validate/describe/apply; setExprRefs, ruleLabel,
  maskSummary. 10 tests, mutation-checked (10/10).
- Tests: studio lib 174 (grammar/planner/coercer additions, capability
  model, insertionPoint; mutation-checked), scripts/mode-sync-test.mjs
  (13: §1, §4, §11, §13), Grid 51, Architect 38, Flow 40, Intelligent
  41, foundation/product-surface/menubar and a 17-suite regression
  batch green.

